<tr>
  <td class="font-medium text-slate-900">
    <%= link_to barcode_item_row.barcodeable.name, barcode_item_path(barcode_item_row), class: "link-brand" %>
  </td>
  <td class="quantity"><%= number_with_delimiter(barcode_item_row.quantity) %></td>
  <td class="font-mono text-xs"><%= barcode_item_row.value %></td>
  <td class="cell-actions">
    <%# Was View, Edit and Delete inline -- 349px, the widest actions column in the app. The View
        goes because the barcode's name in the first cell already links to it, which leaves a
        settled pair that is always both present, so they stay inline: two clicks saved over a
        menu, and the column does not move because nothing here is conditional. %>
    <div class="flex justify-end gap-1.5 whitespace-nowrap">
      <%= essentials_row_icon_link "Edit", edit_barcode_item_path(barcode_item_row), icon: "bi-pencil" %>
      <%= essentials_row_icon_action "Delete", barcode_item_path(barcode_item_row), method: :delete, icon: "bi-trash", tone: :danger,
            confirm: confirm_delete_msg(barcode_item_row.item.name) %>
    </div>
  </td>
</tr>
